-- a citation in an essay's source, (cite NAME "words") (lib/selection.cub), as the page draws it: the words,
-- linked to NAME's place in the human interface. The reference is the definition the checker resolved, so
-- the link cannot point at nothing; the words are exactly what every projection of the text shows (cite-shows).
s-cite-md : List Word → List Word → List Word
s-cite-md n w = h-concat (cons "[" (cons w (cons "](" (cons (hi-href nil n) (cons ")" nil)))))
